{"title":"Andrew Wiles","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><table style=\"border:thin solid black;padding:5px;float:right;margin:10px;\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"border:thin solid gray;\">\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Wiles1.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img alt=\"Andrew Wiles\" src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/f/fc/Wiles1.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"247\" height=\"358\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\t\n</p>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><div class=\"magnify\" style=\"float: right;\">\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Enlarge.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/58/Enlarge.png/15px-Enlarge.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"15\" height=\"9\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/58/Enlarge.png/23px-Enlarge.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/58/Enlarge.png/30px-Enlarge.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure></div> Andrew Wiles\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><b>Andrew Wiles</b> was born on April 11, 1953. Wiles is a Royal Society Research Professor at the University of Oxford, specializing in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Number_theory\" title=\"Number theory\">number theory</a>.   He is most widely known as the mathematician who proved <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Fermat%27s_Last_Theorem\" title=\"Fermat&#39;s Last Theorem\">Fermat's Last Theorem</a>.\n</p><p><br />\n<i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Andrew_Wiles&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018072857\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nC